# Magician patch manifest
#
# Every range of the rebuilt PRG that is filled from the cartridge rather than
# from Eurocom's released source. This file contains **no cartridge bytes**: it
# is a list of claims, each with a digest to check them against, and
# `asm/patches.py` is the only thing that turns a claim into bytes. The cartridge
# is read, never written, and never committed -- see LEGAL.md.
#
# ## Fields
#
#   region <name>   start a region
#   class    a|b|c|d  why the range is filled. See below -- this is the field
#                     that stops a rising match percentage from being
#                     indistinguishable from a rising number of hidden bugs.
#   cart     <dump>  which dump on this machine the bytes come from
#   sha1     <hex>   that dump's body SHA1 (header stripped). Checked against
#                     BOTH the manifest's own registry and the file on disk.
#   prg   <off> <len>  PRG file offset and byte count (hex; `0d` prefix for decimal)
#   cpu      <addr>  the CPU address that offset is presented at, for reading
#   reason   <text>  required. Repeated lines are appended.
#   end            finish the region
#
# ## The four classes
#
#   a  placement bug. The source is right and the module is in the wrong 8 KiB
#      slot. **Fix the placement.** Copying the cartridge over it destroys the
#      only evidence of the bug.
#   b  genuinely absent from the released source. The source is a 02/03/90
#      development build and the cartridge is a 02/1991 one, so this is expected.
#      This is the only class that may be filled from a cartridge.
#   c  assembler bug. The source is present but `asm/pds6502.py` mis-assembles
#      it. **Fix the assembler.**
#   d  data / CHR packing order. A separate problem from code.
#
# Only class `b` regions exist below. Every `a` and `c` region found so far is
# recorded in GAPMAP.md with its evidence and is deliberately *not* filled.

version 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
region sam-samples-at-fc40
class    b
cart     release
sha1     bd806d7f7c318b8012433250ca10aa8387a962bb
prg      1FC40 360
cpu      FC40
reason   X7.PDS:997 says `load mus\sam.sam,$fb80`, and the assembler puts it at
reason   $FB80 as written. It is not there in the cartridge, and the sample data
reason   is at $FC40 instead. Measured: SAM.SAM's first 32 bytes occur exactly
reason   once in the whole 131072-byte PRG, at file $1FC40 (CPU $FC40, the
reason   $E000 fixed window plus $1C40), and the first 864 bytes of
reason   DAT/MUS/SAM.SAM -- all 864 that fit before the cartridge's own $FFF0
reason   title string -- are byte-identical there. $FD9F-$FFEF is zero in the
reason   cartridge, so the range is exactly SAM.SAM[0:$360] and stops short of
reason   `db "MAGIC1+"` at $FFF0.
reason   Class b, not a: this is not a module in the wrong slot, it is an
reason   *address inside a module* that the source states and the release
reason   changed. There is nothing in the source to re-place -- the only honest
reason   description of the difference is that the release moved the samples up
reason   by $C0 bytes and the February 1990 source has the old address.
reason   Effect on the build: X7's own `if last>$fb80 / error ">$FB80!"` guard
reason   (X7.PDS:977-979) is the same stale constant. Because the source still
reason   loads the samples at $FB80, they overwrite 16 bytes of X7's own code
reason   (`last` reaches $FB90), and that 16-byte overrun disappears the moment
reason   this region is filled at the address the cartridge uses.
reason   Not beta-specific, and that is measured rather than assumed: the two
reason   dumps are byte-identical across this whole range. The `cart`/`sha1`
reason   pair is still required on every region, because other ranges of this
reason   cartridge are *not* shared -- 23388 PRG bytes differ overall -- and a
reason   manifest that said only "the cartridge" could be applied to either
reason   dump without complaint.
end
